# beast::unit_test::suite — Detailed Code-Level Explanation

## 1. Class Definition and Core Members

The class is defined as follows (from `include/xrpl/beast/unit_test/suite.h`):

```cpp
class suite
{
private:
    bool abort_ = false;
    bool aborted_ = false;
    runner* runner_ = nullptr;
    // ... (other private members and helper classes)
public:
    log_os<char> log;
    testcase_t testcase;
    static suite this_suite();
    suite();
    virtual ~suite() = default;
    suite(suite const&) = delete;
    suite& operator=(suite const&) = delete;
    // ... (public methods)
};
```

### Member Variables

- `abort_`: Boolean flag indicating if the suite should abort on failure.
- `aborted_`: Boolean flag indicating if the suite has been aborted.
- `runner_`: Pointer to the current test runner.
- `log`: Logging output stream, using a custom log buffer.
- `testcase`: Helper for managing test cases within the suite.

