## 4. Test Execution

### 4.1 operator()(runner& r)

```cpp
template <class>
void suite::operator()(runner& r) {
    p_this_suite() = this;
    try {
        run(r);
        p_this_suite() = nullptr;
    } catch (...) {
        p_this_suite() = nullptr;
        throw;
    }
}
```
- Sets the current suite pointer for the thread.
- Calls `run(r)` (see below).
- Ensures the suite pointer is reset even if an exception occurs.

### 4.2 run(runner& r)

```cpp
template <class>
void suite::run(runner& r) {
    runner_ = &r;
    try {
        run();
    } catch (abort_exception const&) {
        // Aborted, do nothing
    } catch (std::exception const& e) {
        runner_->fail("unhandled exception: " + std::string(e.what()));
    } catch (...) {
        runner_->fail("unhandled exception");
    }
}
```
- Sets the runner pointer.
- Calls the virtual `run()` method (to be implemented by derived test suites).
- Catches `abort_exception` (thrown on abort), and other exceptions, reporting them as failures to the runner.

### 4.3 run() (pure virtual)

```cpp
virtual void run() = 0;
```
- Must be implemented by derived test suites to define the actual test logic.

