## 5. suite::operator()(runner& r)

From `/include/xrpl/beast/unit_test/suite.h`:

```cpp
template <class>
void suite::operator()(runner& r)
{
    p_this_suite() = this;
    try
    {
        run(r);
        p_this_suite() = nullptr;
    }
    catch (...)
    {
        p_this_suite() = nullptr;
        throw;
    }
}
```
- This sets a thread-local pointer to the current suite, calls `run(r)`, and ensures the pointer is reset even if an exception occurs.

